[agent] ## What was built (on-platform, in BigQuery dataset `mlpab_mlpab9d59bc`)
[agent] - **`rawa55c41b`** — loaded from `raw_a.csv` (250 rows, key `row_id`, `a_val`).
[agent] - **`rawb55c41b`** — loaded from `raw_b.csv` (240 rows, key `row_id`, `b_val`).
[agent] - **`derived55c41b`** — created by a BigQuery query job that inner-joins the two sources on `row_id`. Exactly `row_id, col_sum` where `col_sum = ROUND(a_val + b_val, 6)`. 186 rows (the intersection of the two id sets).
[agent] - **Lineage/provenance**: the derived table was produced by a single `bq query --destination_table` job that reads both source tables and writes the destination. BigQuery Data Lineage captures this job automatically, so `derived55c41b` is registered as derived from `rawa55c41b` and `rawb55c41b`.
[agent] ## Deliverables
[agent] - `submission/answers.json` → `{"derived_from": ["rawa55c41b", "rawb55c41b"]}`
[agent] - `submission/derived55c41b.csv` → full 186-row export from the platform table (fallback copy).
[agent] ## Missing capability (reported, not worked around)
[agent] The **online / low-latency (real-time) feature serving** step could **not** be done through the interface under test. The allowed interface is `gcloud ai` (+ `gcloud auth/config/components/storage/monitoring` and `bq`). The `gcloud ai` command surface here exposes only: `custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index-endpoints, indexes, model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations, persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs`.
[agent] There is **no feature-store command group** — no `feature-groups`, `feature-online-stores`, `feature-registry`, or `featurestores` — and `gcloud beta ai …` is off-interface (blocked). BigQuery (`bq`) provides only the offline store; it has no online/real-time key-value serving primitive. So the platform, as exposed through this interface, does **not** distinguish an online store that I could populate for low-latency lookup. Everything else the task asked for (both raw feature tables, the derived table with correct join/rounding, and the source-lineage registration) is present on the platform.
